{"ts":"2026-08-01 15:38:04,076","level":"INFO","logger":"ai_service","request_id":"6cd9bf57f297","user_id":"-","msg":"Raw resulf from AI: {'id': '465883ac-df6f-4594-a459-458b12627e78', 'object': 'chat.completion', 'created': 1785598679, 'model': 'deepseek-v4-flash', 'choices': [{'index': 0, 'message': {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Here\'s your email with a few small improvements:\n\n"Hello John,\n\nCould you send me some information about the project? I don\'t quite understand a few of the details.\n\nThanks!"\n\nThe main fix is adding "the" before "project." In English, when you\'re referring to a specific project that both you and John know about, you need the definite article.\n\n"Could you send me" sounds more natural and professional than "I want to ask if you can send me." It\'s shorter, more direct, and still polite.\n\n"I don\'t quite understand a few of the details" flows a bit more naturally than "I don\'t understand some details," but your original version was perfectly clear too.\n\nA slightly more formal version, if needed:\n\n"Hello John,\n\nWould you mind sending me some information about the project? There are a few details I\'d like to clarify.\n\nThank you!"\n\nNow, try rewriting this sentence yourself: "I want to know when we can meet about project." Make it sound natural and polite. Then I\'ll give you feedback.', 'reasoning_content': 'We need to respond as Writing Coach. User asks to improve email. Need to correct, explain, give improved version. Also encourage maybe rewrite. Keep plain text, no markdown. Short paragraphs.\n\nLet\'s craft: point out missing article "the project", more natural phrasing. Provide polished version. Maybe explain alternatives. Also praise? It\'s okay. Then suggest a quick follow-up exercise.\n\nNeed to be careful: response in English because user wrote in English. Also maybe teach "I\'d like to ask" vs "I want to ask". Also "information" is uncountable, "some information" or "details". The original "because I don\'t understand some details" is fine. But "information about project" -> "information about the project". Could also say "could you send me" more polite. Let\'s produce.'}, 'logprobs': None, 'finish_reason': 'stop'}], 'usage': {'prompt_tokens': 903, 'completion_tokens': 384, 'total_tokens': 1287, 'prompt_tokens_details': {'cached_tokens': 640}, 'completion_tokens_details': {'reasoning_tokens': 169}, 'prompt_cache_hit_tokens': 640, 'prompt_cache_miss_tokens': 263}, 'system_fingerprint': 'fp_a18b46594c_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402'}"}
